---
title: "Row Grouping - Hierarchy Selection"
enterprise: true
---

Row Selection can be configured with groups to select all of a rows descendants.

## Selecting Descendants

When using [Multiple Row Selection](./row-selection-multi-row/) with row grouping, the grid can be configured to impact descendant and
ancestor rows when a row is selected.

To enable hierarchical selection, set the `selection.groupSelects` option to one of the following values:

- `'self'`: Selecting a group row has no additional side effects.
- `'descendants'`: Selecting a group row will select all of its descendants.
- `'filteredDescendants'`: Selecting a group row will select all of its descendants that pass the filter.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Group Selection" name="group-selection" /%}

The example above demonstrates the following configuration:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowSelection: {
        mode: 'multiRow',
        groupSelects: 'descendants',
    },
}
```

{% note %}
When using `groupSelects: 'descendants'` or `groupSelects: 'filteredDescendants'`, group nodes will not be returned as part of `api.getSelectedNodes()` or `api.getSelectedRows()`.
{% /note %}

## Selecting Total Rows

A [Total Row](./aggregation-total-rows/) has no selection of its own. Selecting a group total row selects its group, and selecting the grand total row selects the root node. This applies to clicks, the keyboard and the API:

- The grid's `rowSelected` event is raised for the group node or the root node, never for the total row. The root node has `level` `-1`.
- A total row's `isSelected()` returns the selection of its group or of the root node.
- `api.setNodesSelected` accepts a total row and selects or deselects its group or the root node.
- With `groupSelects: 'self'`, `api.getSelectedNodes()` returns the group node or the root node. `api.getSelectedRows()` returns only the selected nodes that have `data`, and the root node has none, so selecting the grand total row adds no row to it.
- With `groupSelects` set to `'descendants'` or `'filteredDescendants'`, selecting a group total row also selects the group's descendants, and selecting the grand total row selects every row. With the Client-Side Row Model, `api.getSelectedNodes()` then returns the selected rows without their groups or the root node; the Server-Side Row Model does not support it in these modes.
- With the [Server-Side Row Model](./server-side-model-selection/), `api.getServerSideSelectionState()` names the root node `ROOT_NODE_ID`.

A group total row can be selected when its group can. `isRowSelectable` is called with the grand total row itself (`footer` is `true`), and its result decides whether the root node can be selected. With the Client-Side Row Model and `groupSelects` set to `'descendants'` or `'filteredDescendants'`, it is not called with the grand total row, which can be selected when any of its rows can, as groups are. With the Server-Side Row Model and `groupSelects: 'descendants'`, a group for which it returns `false` still shows the selection of its rows, and a rejected group or grand total row can be deselected through the API.

## Checkboxes in Group Cells

When using [Row Selection](./row-selection/) with grouping, the grid can be configured to render checkboxes in the group cell, to
the right of the expand/collapse chevron.

This can be configured on by setting the `rowSelection.checkboxLocation` option to `'autoGroupColumn'`.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Group Cell Checkboxes" name="group-cell-checkboxes" /%}

The example above demonstrates the following configuration to render checkboxes in the group cell:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowSelection: {
        mode: 'multiRow',
        checkboxLocation: 'autoGroupColumn',
    },
}
```
